# Client Renderer (`client.js`)

The browser draws the game. It does **not** decide who wins a fight.

## Allowed
- UI clicks that **emit** intents to the server (`JOIN_GAME`, `NAVIGATE_TO`, `submit-turn`, etc.)
- Path preview for the player (server still validates the real path)
- Rendering from `STATE_SYNC`, `ROOM_TRANSITION`, `resolve-round`, and related server events

## Forbidden without explicit request
- Local combat damage math that becomes “truth”
- Skipping screens or changing room state without a server event
- Changing gold / HP / party composition locally as authoritative state

## Patch style
- Touch only the UI / listener / draw function you need.
- Keep socket listener names and payload shapes aligned with the server.
- Comment non-obvious UI state flags (e.g. `isWaitingForCombatResolution`) in plain English.
